// Title: Touch Suspicious Service File
// Sigma ID: 31545105-3444-4584-bebf-c466353230d2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Joseliyo Sanchez, @Joseliyo_Jstnk
// Date: 2023-01-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070.006
// Description: Detects usage of the "touch" process in service file.
// False positives:
//   - Admin changing date of files.
// References:
//   - https://blogs.blackberry.com/
//   - https://twitter.com/Joseliyo_Jstnk/status/1620131033474822144
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_touch_susp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/touch" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -t " and ProcessCommandLine endswith ".service"
